{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641943,"nonce":"XQ2hzyF0Eb9blDuZOYY8vgY5+hI=","title":"ZYNTAX_TRACE_LAZY read with env::var_os on every stub call","message":"osr.rs lazy_interpret and note_lazy_declined call std::env::var_os(\"ZYNTAX_TRACE_LAZY\") on every stub call to a function without code yet (getenv under the env lock plus an environment scan). They do not cache it in a OnceLock\u003cbool\u003e as osr_trace_enabled does. The stub-interpreter closure also takes two Mutexes (eligible, asked) and a view RwLock read per call.\n\nEach native call into a function without code pays the environment scan, up to the warm count per function and again for every declined call while its compile is pending. The comment on osr_probe in the same file records the same pattern costing about half of a loop's wall time on macOS.\n\nDirection: cache the flag in a OnceLock\u003cbool\u003e.","files":null}]}